From: Cubewood <330162352+Cubewood@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 23:09:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Junction mouths of narrow roads: cores at least 6.5 m from
 the centreline near a junction

The junction-mouth blend reaches as far as the road cores (half width plus
the 1 m shoulder), so the narrower the roads the shorter the warp from one
road's grade to the other's. A 6 m street falling at 15 % into a 7 m road
changed grade within two metres of the mouth, where a turning car runs.
Within a junction (a node three or more roads share on the ground) a road's
core is now at least MOUTH_CORE_M (6.5 m) from its centreline for 6 m along
it from the node, narrowing back to its own over the next 6 m. The blend,
ownership and side slopes all use that core. Service roads and tracks keep
their own core: a level driveway widened that way pulled a climbing street's
lanes off its grade along 12 m.

